$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5,6-Di-O-(4-chlorobenzoyl)-1-N-tert-butoxycarbonyl-3,2’,6’-triazido-3’,4’-dideoxy-3’-
enoneamine (4). To a solution of the di-acylated compound, 3 (0.20g, 0.29
mmol), BOC-ON (0.17 g, 0.71 mmol) in 10 mL anhydrous toluene at -78°C
under nitrogen, PMe3 (1.0 M solution in toluene) (0.32 mL, 0.32 mmol) was
added. The reaction was kept at -78°C for 30 minutes, then was allowed to
warm to -10°C. The reaction was quenched with phophate buffer (pH = 7.4)
and was concentrated. The residue was extracted with EtOAc. The organic
layer was washed with 1N HCl(aq), H2O, saturated NaHCO3(aq), and brine,
then dried over Na2SO4 (s). Removal of the solvent followed by
purification with gradient column chromatography (Hexanes:EtOAc = 100:0
to 40:60) afforded the desired product (0.11 g, 0.14 mmol, 84%). 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.2 – 7.8 (m, 8H), 5.8 (d, J = 10.5 Hz, 1H, H-3’), 5.7
(d, J = 10.5 Hz, 1H, H-4’), 5.6 (dd, J = 9.7 Hz, J = 9.7Hz, 1H, H-5 ),
5.27 (d, J = 5.6 Hz, 1H, H-1'), 5.1 (dd, J = 10.2 Hz, J = 10.3 Hz, 1H,
H-6), 4.6 – 4.8 (m, 1H, H-5), 3.92 (dd, J = 9.6 Hz, J = 9.7 Hz, 1H, H-4),
3.72 (dd, J = 6.4 Hz, J = 5.8 Hz, 1H, H-1 ), 3.43 (ddd, J = 3.4 Hz, J =
9.0 Hz, J = 3.7 Hz, 1H, H-2’), 3.26 (ddd, J = 5.7 Hz, J = 12.8 Hz, J =
7.1 Hz, 1H, H-6’), 2.53 (ddd, J = 13.1 Hz, J = 4.3 Hz, J = 4.0 Hz, 1H,
H-2eq), 1.62 (ddd, J = 12.7 Hz, J = 12.8 Hz, J = 12.5 Hz, 1H, H-2ax),
1.24 (s, 9H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 165.8 (s), 164.2 (s), 155.0 (s),
140.2 (s, 2 carbons), 139.9 (s),131.4 (s, 2 carbons), 130.9 (s), 129.3
(s), 129.0 (s), 128.8 (s), 127.6 (s), 127.0 (s), 122.9 (s), 98.1 (s),
80.3 (s), 78.4 (s), 77.5 (s), 77.0 (s), 76.6 (s), 74.5 (s), 74.3 (s),
68.8 (s), 68.0 (s), 59.6 (s), 54.3 (s), 54.0 (s), 33. 6 (s),28.1 (s),
25.6 (s). MALDI Calcd for C31H32Cl2N10O8Na ([M+Na]+) m/e 765.1674;
measure m/e 765.1655.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, buffered solution, phosphate buffer used in last stage
