$DATUM 1310-73-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of 3b (16.6 mg, 0.0440 mmol) in 0.5 mL 3:1 DMF-phosphate
buffer was added a solution of 4 (6.50 mg, 0.049 mmol) in the same
solvent 0.4 mL at room temperature. After 30 min, conc. HCl was added to
the reaction flask (total c = 6 M). The deprotection was monitored
completed within 20 min. The reaction mixture was transferred into a
sep-funnel and diluted with water. The mixture was extracted with EtOAc
one time. The aqueous layer was adjusted to pH 8-9 with 10% NaOH, and
then extracted with ethyl acetate twice (2 × 10 mL). The combined organic
layers were dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo to
afford a desired amine. Pale yellow oil, yield (15 mg, 84 %), 12. 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.97 (br-s, 1H), 7.45 - 7.15 (m, 5H), 4.43 (d, J = 6.0
Hz, 2H), 3.79 (dd, J = 9.1, 5.3 Hz, 1H), 2.99 (dt, J = 10.2, 6.8 Hz, 1H),
2.86 (dt, J = 10.2, 6.3 Hz, 1H), 2.31 (br-s, 1H), 2.26 - 2.07 (m, 1H),
2.03 - 1.88 (m, 1H), 1.79 - 1.64 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ
175.32, 138.90, 128.84, 127.80, 127.51, 60.81, 47.49, 43.13, 31.06,
26.46; IR (thin film) 3313.5, 3064.2, 3027.5, 2958.0, 2945.7, 2876.3,
1654.5, 1511.5, 14461.1, 731.0, 698.3 cm-1; MS (ESI) m/z calcd for
C12H17N2O [M+H]+ 205.1, found 205.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM phosphate buffered solution used, Staudinger ligation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A proline-based phosphine template for Staudinger ligation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Park, Chung-Min; Niu, Wei; Liu, Chunrong; Biggs, Tyler D.; Guo, Jiantao;
Xian, Ming
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(17), 4694-4697

