$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure: A solution of azide (1.0
eq) and phosphine (1.1 eq for 7 and 0.55 eq for 8 and 9) in THF (0.1 M)
was heated at reflux for 2 h. The solution was treated with water (100
μL/0.1 mmol of azide) and heated at reflux overnight. The solution was
cooled to 23 °C then diluted with THF (0.02 M relative to phosphine) and
treated with erythrosin B (5 mol% relative to phosphine). The solution
was irradiated with a 250 W sunlamp (4 h for 7, 2 h for 8, 1 h for 9).
After irradiation, the solution was treated with MP-Carbonate (50 eq
relative to erythrosin B) and the reaction mixture was stirred for 2 h to
remove erythrosin B. Volatile components of the reaction mixture were
removed in vacuo. The amines were extracted from the crude solids with
Et2O (1-3 mL/0.1 mmol of azide) and filtered through a 0.45 μm filter.
Volatile components of the filtrate were removed in vacuo to leave
remaining the amines (yields indicated in Tables 1 and 2).
3-(4-tert-Butyl-phenoxy)-propylamine:9 yield: 83%. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.31 (d, J = 8.9 Hz, 2 H); 6.85 (d, J = 8.9 Hz, 2 H); 4.04 (t, J
= 6.1 Hz, 2 H); 2.91 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 2 H); 1.97-1.90 (m, 2 H), 1.31 (s, 9
H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical (in stage 2), Mp-carbonate used in last stage
