$DATUM N-Benzyl-4-fluorobenzamide (14)30 Benzyl azide (11;31 60 mg, 0.45 mmol)
and phosphane 4b (150 mg, 0.37 mmol) were dissolved in a DMF-H2O mixture
(0.5 mL:0.05 mL) and heated under microwave conditions (50 Watt) for 20
min. After removal of the solvent under reduced pressure, the crude
product was purified by column chromatography (PE-EtOAc, 20:1). Colorless
crystals, yield 71 mg, 83%. Mp 143-144 °C; Rf = 0.41 (PE-EtOAc, 1:1). 1H
NMR (400 MHz, C6D6): δ = 4.40 (d, 2J = 5.6 Hz, 2 H, CH2), 5.71 (br s, 1
H, NH), 6.64 (t, 3Jo,m = 3JH,F = 8.6 Hz, 1 H, Hm), 7.02-7.13 (m, 5 H,
C6H5), 7.37 (dd, 3Jo,m = 8.6 Hz, 4JH,F = 5.5 Hz, 1 H, Ho). 13C NMR (101
MHz, C6D6): δ = 44.0 (CH2N), 115.4 (d, 2JC,F = 22.1 Hz, C-3/C-5), 127.6
(Cp), 128.1 (Cm), 128.8 (C-1), 129.7 (d, 3JC,F = 8.8 Hz, C-2/C-6), 139.2
(Cipso), 165.5 (C=O), 167.4 (d, 1JC,F = 250.5 Hz, C-4). 19F NMR (376 MHz,
C6D6): δ = -109.5. MS (ESI+): m/z (%) = 230 (12, [M+ + H]), 252 (100, [M+
+ Na]). Anal. Calcd for C14H12FNO: C, 73.35; H, 5.28; N, 6.11. Found: C,
73.61; H, 5.45; N, 6.14.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, heated
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
