$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Thiazoline 12d. To a stirred solution of azide
11d (51 mg, 78 μmol) in THF (5 mL) was added triphenylphosphine (30.5 mg,
0.116 mmol). The reaction mixture was heated and maintained at 50 °C for
12 h. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure and the residue was
purified by siica gel column chromatography (hexanes-ethyl acetate, 12:1,
v/v) to yield the 12d (32 mg, 67%) as a colorless oil. yield 82%.
Compound No: 12b.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Staudinger reduction/aza-Wittig reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of the Apratoxin 2,4-Disubstituted Thiazoline via an
Intramolecular Aza-Wittig Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chen, Jiehao; Forsyth, Craig J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2003), 5(8), 1281-1283

