$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (Z)-methyl
N-6-amino-9-((2R,5S)-3,4-dihydroxy-5-(hydroxymethyl)-tetrahydrofuran-2-yl)-9H-purin-8-yl-2-(diphenylphosphoryl)-4-((2-(2-(2-(4-pyren-1-yl)butanamido)ethoxy)ethoxy)ethyl)carbamoyl)benzimidate
(9a). To 8-azidoadenosine 7 (0.0123 g, 0.0400 mmol) in 1.0 mL 1:1 THF/H2O
was added pyrene phosphine 6a (0.0306 g, 0.0400 mmol) in 1.0 mL 1:1
THF/H2O. The reaction was incubated at 30°C for 2h. The reaction mixture
was extracted with ethyl acetate, washed with brine, and dried over
Na2SO4. The solvent was removed and the resulting material purified by
flash chromatography [3:2 EtOAc:Hex.] to yield 9a as a light yellowish
oil (34 mg, 82% yield). TLC and HPLC-MS revealed this material to be
identical to that identified during the course of HPLC timetrial
analyses. (Z)-methyl
N-6-amino-9-((2R,5S)-3,4-dihydroxy-5-(hydroxymethyl)-tetrahydrofuran-2-yl)-9H-purin-8-yl-2-(diphenylphosphoryl)-4-((2-(2-(2-(4-pyren-1-yl)butanamido)ethoxy)ethoxy)ethyl)carbamoyl)benzimidate
(9a). (34 mg, 82% yield). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 8.37 (d, J= 14.4 Hz, 1H), 8.24
(d, J= 9.6 Hz, 1H), 8.14-7.94 (m, 9H), 7.87-7.80 (m, 5H), 7.53-7.42 (m,
5H), 6.56 (d, J= 7.2 Hz, 1H), 5.01 (dd, J= 6.8, 5.2 Hz, 1H), 4.48 (d, J=
5.2 Hz, 1H), 4.30 (s, 1H), 3.96 (d, J= 12.8 Hz, 1H), 3.73-3.25 (m, 27H),
2.27-2.01 (m, 4H). 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 173.01, 167.75, 166.38, 154.75,
151.58, 148.67, 147.89, 135.70, 135.61, 132.72, 130.75, 130.66, 131.81,
128.95, 128.55, 126.68, 126.30, 125.68, 125.05, 124.63, 124.15, 120.62,
70.42, 70.36, 70.15, 69.79, 68.20, 52.44, 50.97, 40.01, 39.42, 36.22,
33.05, 27.66, 25.87. 31P NMR (CDCl3) δ 22.6. HRMS (MALDI): calcd for
C357H57N8O10P [M+Na] = 1067.3833, measured 1067.3420.
