$DATUM 3’-[(N-tert-Butoxycarbonyl-O-methyl)-L-tyrosyl]amido-3’-deoxyinosine 9: A
mixture of Boc-Tyr(Me)-OH (19 mg, 0.06 mmol) and HOBt (10mg, 0.07 mmol)
was coevaporated from anhydrous THF. This solution (2.5 mL) was cooled
down to 0°C under N2 for 10 min, then DIC (10 μL, 0.06 mmol) was added.
After 10 min 8 (16 mg, 0.05 mmol) and (nBu)3P (30 μL, 0.12 mmol) were
added. The reaction mixture was stirred at rt overnight then H2O (1 mL)
and MeOH (1 mL) were added. The reaction mixture was then concentrated in
vacuo under reduced pressure. The residue was purified on a silica gel
column (EtOAc, EtOAc/MeOH/H2O 9:0.5:0.5, EtOAc/ MeOH/H2O 9:1:1) to give
~24 mg (82%) of 9 as a white amorphous solid after lyophilisation from
water.
3’-[(N-tert-Butoxycarbonyl-O-methyl)-L-tyrosyl]amido-3’-deoxyinosine 9,
yield ~24 mg (82%). C25H32N6O8: 544.57. M.r. 118-122°C; Rf = 0.48 (EtOAc/
MeOH/H2O 9:1:1); 1H NMR (CD3OD): δ = 8.35, 8.06 (2s, 2H, H-8 and H-2);
7.13, 6.82 (2d, 4H, J = 8.5, C6H4-Tyr); 6.00 (d, 1H, 3J(1’,2’) = 5.4,
H-1’); 4.95 (t, 1H, 3J = 5.5, H-2’); 4.30-4.27 (m, 2H, H-3’ + CH-α);
4.13-4.11 (m, 1H, H-4’); 3.87 (dd, 1H, J = 2.8, J = 12.5, H-5’); 3.75 (s,
3H, OCH3); 3.75-3.72 (m, 1H, H-5”); 3.08 (dd, 1H, 2J(β1,β2) = 13.9,
3J(α,β) = 4.9, H-β1); 2.88-2.81 (m, 1H, H-β2); 13C NMR (CD3OD): δ =
174.9, 160.0, 158.8, 157.8, 149.7, 146.8, 140.9, 131.3, 130.6, 126.0,
114.8, 90.5, 84.9, 80.4, 76.8, 63.4, 62.8, 56.7, 55.6, 38.0, 28.7; HRMS
(ESI+): m/z : calculated for C25H33N6O8: 545.2360; found: 545.2362
[M+H]+.
