$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Carboxylic acid 18 A solution of anhydride 17 and trimethylphosphine (3.6
mL, 1.0 M in toluene, 3.60 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (60 mL) was stirred for 3 h at
room temperature and the solvent removed. The residue was purified by
flash chromatography (hexanes-ethyl acetate, 1:1) to afford 0.82 g (82%)
of acid 18 as a white solid: Carboxylic acid 18, yield 0.82 g 82%. mp
100-102 °C; IR (neat) 2950, 2929, 2859, 1819, 1719; 1H-NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 5.88 (m, 2H), 4.21 (d, J = 5.0 Hz, 1H), 3.77 (ddd, J = 17.5,
6.0, 3.0 Hz, 1H), 3.68 (ddd, J = 17.5, 9.0, 6.5 Hz, 1H), 2.81 (dd, J =
19.5, 2 Hz, 1H), 2.70 (dd, J = 10.0, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 2.33 (ddd, J = 19.5,
10.0, 3.5 Hz, 1H), 1.82 (m, 2H), 1.77 (m, 1H), 1.54 (m, 1H), 0.84 (s,
9H), 0.03 (s, 3H), 0.00 (s, 3H); 13 C-NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 173.5,
165.1, 128.2, 126.5, 66.1, 46.5, 45.3, 43.0, 28.9, 25.4, 19.9, 19.4,
17.8, -4.3, -5.3; MS(ESI) m/z , 338.1758 [(M-H)+, cald for C17H28NO4Si,
338.1788].
