$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of Alkyl
5-Alkoxy- 4,4-dialkyl-2-oxopyrrolidine-3-carboxylates (15). To a solution
of azidocyclopropane 9 (1 mmol) in dry THF (4 mL) under nitrogen
atmosphere was added Ph3P (0.275 g, 1.05 mmol). The reaction mixture was
stirred for 3 h at r.t. The reaction mixture was poured into H2O (10 mL)
and extracted with CH2Cl2. After drying of the organic layer (MgSO4),
filtration and evaporation, the pure pyrrolidin-2-ones 15 were obtained
as diastereomeric mixtures after column chromatography (silica gel,
PE-EtOAc). Pyrrolidinone 15a. 15c , Yield 81 %.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 2:1 diastereomers, Staudinger reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Michael-induced ring closure to 2-azidocyclopropane-1,1-dicarboxylates
and their Staudinger reduction to
5-alkoxy-3-(alkoxycarbonyl)pyrrolidin-2-ones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mangelinckx, Sven; De Kimpe, Norbert
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2006), (3), 369-374

