$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Method B (DCC coupling). Compound 2 (500 mg, 2.15 mmol) and
N-acetylphenylalanine (446 mg, 2.15 mmol) were dissolved in DMF (15 mL)
under Ar(g). 1,3-Dicyclohexylcarbodiimide (DCC; 489 mg, 2.37 mmol) was
then added, and the reaction mixture was stirred for 12 h at room
temperature. The 1,3-dicyclohexylurea (DCU) by-product was removed by
filtration, solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the residue
was purified by chromatography as in Method A. AcPheSCH2PPh2 was isolated
as a white solid in 84% yield. Spectral data. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ
7.44-7.39 (m, 4 H), 7.35-7.33 (m, 6 H), 7.26-7.21 (m, 3 H), 7.11-7.09 (m,
2 H), 6.29 (d,J= 8.4 Hz, 1 H), 4.98-4.91 (m, 1 H), 3.57-3.44 (m, 2 H),
3.09 (dd,J= 14.1, 5.4 Hz, 1 H), 2.93 (dd,J= 14.1, 7.5 Hz, 1 H) 1.88 (s, 3
H) ppm; 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ 198.91, 169.86, 135.50, 132.62 (d,J=
19.4 Hz), 129.11 (d,J= 9.8 Hz) 128.79 (d,J= 35.9 Hz), 128.50, 128.45,
126.99, 59.56, 37.99, 25.61 (d,J= 24.4 Hz), 22.88 ppm; 31P NMR (CDCl3,
121 MHz) -44.66 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
