$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure A (release as amine): The
iminophosphorane-loaded resin was swollen in 10% water in DMF
(approximately 8 mL per g resin) and heated either thermally at 40
&#x00B0;C overnight or with &#x3BC;w irradiation at 60 &#x00B0;C (2 x 10
min). The resin then was filtered and washed with DMF (6 x 2 min) to
extract the released amine. The combined filtrates were concentrated and
freeze-dried in order to determine reaction yield and product purity.
6I-amino-6-II-VII-hexaazido-6I-VII-heptadeoxy-2I-VII,3I-VII-tetradeca-O-methylcyclomaltoheptaose
(10). Monoamine 10 was obtained from 3 (153 mg, 0.1 mmol, 2 eq) and resin
7 (0.15 g, 0.34 mmol·g-1) using the catch-and-release protocol as
described in procedure A in 79% yield (60 mg). HPLC: tR = 9.2 min;
ESI-MS: m/z 1480.8 [M + Na]+. Rf = 0.50 (9:1 DCM-MeOH); [&#x3B1;]D =
+149.1 (c 1.0, DCM); 1H NMR (500 MHz, MeOD, 333 K): &#x3B4; 5.27 (d, 1 H,
J1,2 = 3.7 Hz, H-1II), 5.22-5.18 (m, 6 H, H-1I,III-VII), 3.95-3.84 (m, 11
H, H-5II-VII, H-6aII-VI), 3.81-3.78 (dd, 1 H, H-6aVII), 3.77-3.74 (ddd, 1
H, H-5I), 3.70-3.50 (m, 20 H, H-4I-VII, H-3I-VII, H-6bII-VII), 3.66 (m,
21 H, OCH3 I-VII), 3.55 (m, 21 H, OCH3 I-VII), 3.26-3.21 (m, 7 H,
H-2I-VII), 3.19-3.16 (dd, 1 H, H-6aI), 3.07-3.02 (dd, 1 H, H-6bI);
1D-TOCSY (500 MHz, MeOD, H-6aI irradiation): &#x3B4; 5.21 (d, 1 H, J1,2 =
2.8 Hz, H-1I), 3.75 (ddd, 1 H, J4,5 = 8.4 Hz, J5,6a= 2.9 Hz, J5,6b = 5.6
Hz, H-5I), 3.58-3.52 (m, 2 H, H-3I, H-4I), 3.22 (dd, 1 H, J2,3 = 8.6 Hz,
H-2I), 3.16 (dd, 1 H, H-6a), 3.04 (dd, 1 H, H-6b, J6a,6b = 14.0 Hz);
1D-TOCSY (500 MHz, MeOD, H-2II irradiation): &#x3B4; 5.25 (d, 1 H, J1,2 =
3.9 Hz, H-1II), 3.92 (ddd, 1 H, H-5 II), 3.85 (d, 1 H, H-6aII), 3.69 (dd,
1 H, J6a,6b = 14.0 Hz, J5,6b = 4.0 Hz, H-6b II), 3.6 (t, 1 H, H-4 II),
3.52 (t, 1 H, J2,3 = J3,4 = 9.1 Hz, H-3 II), 3.23 (dd, 1 H, J2,3 = 9.9
Hz, H-2 II); 13C NMR (125.7 MHz, MeOD): &#x3B4; 100.6-100.4 (C-1I-VII),
84.0-82.1 (C-2I-VII, C-3I-VII, C-4I-VII), 73.8-73.2 (C-5I-VII), 62.8-62.4
(OCH3), 60.2-59.9 (OCH3), 54.1-53.9 (C-6II-VII), 43.9 (C-6I); ESI-MS: m/z
1480.6 [M + H]+, 1502.1 [M + Na]+. Elemental analysis calculated (%) for
C56H93N19O28: C 45.43, H 6.33, N 17.98; found: C 45.08, H 6.27, N 17.61.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (40W) (stage 1), alternative reaction conditions
shown, sealed glass vial used (stage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Implementing the "Catch-and-Release" Concept into a Simple Method for
Regioselective Cyclodextrin Modification
