$DATUM {η5-C5H4-(PPh2=N-2,6-Me2-C6H3)}Fe{η5-C5H3-1-(PPh2=N-2,6-Me2-C6H3-2-CH(Me)OMe}
(2c). To a solution of BPPFA-OMe (1.00 g, 1.18 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (10 mL)
was added drop wise 2,6-dimethylbenzoyl azide (0.50 g, 2. 58
mmol).Bubbles of N2 gas evolved during the addition. The mixture was
stirred for 6 h at ambient temperature, after which time the solvent was
removed under vacuum. The oily residue dissolved in a minimum amount of
CH2Cl2 was transferred into a column of silica gel for chromatographic
separation. A single orange band was eluted with a mixture of hexane and
ethyl acetate (7:3) to give orange solids after removal of solvents. Re
crystallization from CH2Cl2/hexane yielded 1.03g of 2c (79%) in two crops
as orange solids.
{η5-C5H4-(PPh2=N-2,6-Me2-C6H3)}Fe{η5-C5H3-1-(PPh2=N-2,6-Me2-C6H3-2-CH(Me)OMe}
(2c). yield79% 31P NMR (CDCl3): δ -8.96, -8.20 (s, P=N). 1H NMR (CDCl3):
δ 1.23 (d, J = 6.3, 3H, CHMe), 2.02, 2.05 (s, 12H, Me2-Ph), 2.55 (s, 3H,
OMe), 4.13 (qt, J = 7.2, 1H, CHMe), 4.49, 4.53 (m, 4H, C5H4), 3.82, 4.51,
4.85 (br, 3H, C5H3), 6.02 (m, 2H, C6H3), 6.90 (m, 4H, M-C6H3), 7.28-7.60
(m, 20H, PPh2). Anal. Calcd for C53H52-FeN2OP2: C, 74.82; H, 6.16; N,
3.29. Found: C, 74.86; H, 6.45; N, 3.02.
