$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Compound S18-1 (56 mg, 0.0523 mmol) and PPh3
(27 mg, 0.1046 mmol) were dissolved in benzene (600 μL) and H2O (6 μL).
Then, the mixture was stirred at 60°C for 12 h. After completion of
reaction monitored by TLC, the reaction mixture was condensed under
reduced pressure and re-dissolved in anhydrous THF (300 μL). Cerotic acid
(48 mg, 0.1203 mmol), EDCI (23 mg, 0.1203 mmol) and DMAP (catalytic
amount) were added to the corresponding mixture and stirred at r.t. for
24 h. After reaction completion, the resulting mixture was diluted with
EtOAc and washed with brine. The combined organic layer was dried over
anhydrous Na2SO4(s). The filtrate was condensed under reduced pressure
and purified by silica-gel flash column chromatography (EtOAc : Hex = 1 :
3, v/v) to provide the desired product S19-1. Compound S19-3 was
synthesized from 18-3 (30 mg, 27.5 μmol) with the identical procedure for
S19-1 as a colorless oil. Two step yield: 31 mg (78%). [α]D20 -2.9 (c =
0.31, CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.58 (s, 1H), 7.43 (s, 1H),
7.36-7.18 (m, 30H), 7.12-7.08 (m, 4H), 6.07 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1H), 5.23 (d,
J = 15.0 Hz, 1H), 5.19 (d, J = 15.0 Hz, 1H), 4.91 (d, J = 11.5 Hz, 1H),
4.80-4.76 (m, 3H), 4.71 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H), 4.66 (d, J = 11.0 Hz, 1H),
4.62 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H), 4.55 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H), 4.51 (d, J = 11.5
Hz, 1H), 4.46-4.44 (m, 3H), 4.35 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H), 4.20 (d, J = 12.0
Hz, 1H), 4.13-4.08 (m, 1H), 4.02 (dd, J = 10.0, 3.5 Hz, 1H), 3.94- 3.85
(m, 5H), 3.55 (dd, J = 10.8, 3.8 Hz, 1H), 3.48 (dd, J = 9.2, 6.8 Hz, 1H),
3.35 (dd, J = 9.5, 6.0 Hz, 1H), 2.55 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H), 1.95-1.83 (m,
2H), 1.56 (quin, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 1.46 (quin, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 1.31-1.25
(m, 50H), 0.92-0.85 (m, 6H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 172.9, 140.2,
138.8, 138.7, 138.6, 137.9, 129.0, 128.6, 128.6, 128.5, 128.5, 128.5,
