$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 6-Triphenylphosphazo-1H-phenalen-1-one (Ic). To a solution of 1.11 g (5
mmol) of azide Ib in 25 ml of methylene chloride was added dropwise at
stirring 1.5 g (5.7 mmol) of triphenylphosphine in 25 ml of methylene
chloride. The mixture was heated under reflux for 1 h, then the solvent
was removed in a vacuum and the residue was heated with 40 ml of hexane
for removing triphenylphosphine excess. The crude product was
chromatographed on silica gel (eluent chloroform). Yield 1.78 g, 78%,
cherry-red crystals. mp 155-156°C. 31P NMR spectrum, δP 8.25 ppm
(ethanol), Rf 0.72 (1), 0.83 (2), 0.45 (3). Found, %: C 80.32, 80.58; H
4.35, 4.46; P 6.23, 6.31; N 2.96, 2.73. C31H22NOP. Calculated, %: C
81.74; H 4.87; P 6.8; N 3.08.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of triphenylphosphazoperiindenones by Staudinger reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
